        "question": {
          ":question/id": "6985fee9-72f3-5576-85b8-e1b8d36aee8e",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
          ":question/problem": "At which points on the curve $x^{2} + 2 x + y^{2} + 1=25$ is a tangent vector perpendicular to $\\mathbf v=\\langle 4,-3\\rangle$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Set $F(x,y)=x^{2} + 2 x + y^{2} + 1$, so the curve is $F(x,y)=25$. A tangent vector is $\\mathbf t=\\langle F_y,-F_x\\rangle$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF_x&=2 x + 2\\\\\nF_y&=2 y\\\\\n\\mathbf t(x,y)&=\\langle 2 y,- 2 x - 2\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPerpendicularity requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf t\\cdot \\langle 4,-3\\rangle&=0\\\\\n6 x + 8 y + 6&=0\\\\\n2 (3 x + 4 y + 3)&=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe condition gives $y=- \\frac{3 x}{4} - \\frac{3}{4}$. Substitution into the original curve gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{25 x^{2}}{16} + \\frac{25 x}{8} + \\frac{25}{16}&=25\\\\\n\\frac{25 (x - 3) (x + 5)}{16}&=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence $x=-5$ or $x=3$. Recovering the other coordinate gives $(-5,3)$ and $(3,-3)$.\n\nThus the qualifying points are $(3,-3)$ and $(-5,3)$. All listed points lie on the curve. The following nonzero tangent vectors check every choice:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf t(4,0)&=\\langle 0,-10\\rangle,\\qquad \\mathbf t\\cdot \\langle 4,-3\\rangle=30\\\\\n\\mathbf t(-6,0)&=\\langle 0,10\\rangle,\\qquad \\mathbf t\\cdot \\langle 4,-3\\rangle=-30\\\\\n\\mathbf t(2,4)&=\\langle 8,-6\\rangle,\\qquad \\mathbf t\\cdot \\langle 4,-3\\rangle=50\\\\\n\\mathbf t(-4,-4)&=\\langle -8,6\\rangle,\\qquad \\mathbf t\\cdot \\langle 4,-3\\rangle=-50\\\\\n\\mathbf t(3,-3)&=\\langle -6,-8\\rangle,\\qquad \\mathbf t\\cdot \\langle 4,-3\\rangle=0\\\\\n\\mathbf t(-5,3)&=\\langle 6,8\\rangle,\\qquad \\mathbf t\\cdot \\langle 4,-3\\rangle=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
